FIRST UI

# Recommended Workflow (with Stripe or PayPal):
Frontend shows a payment form after job creation.

User selects method: credit card or PayPal.

Frontend collects info → uses Stripe.js or PayPal SDK to tokenize securely.

Frontend sends the token + jobId + method to your backend.

Backend stores tokenized method (no sensitive info).

Backend flags job.paymentVerified = true and updates the job record.

# Escrow-Based Funding:

Job is created.

Payment method is set.

Client is prompted to fund the job or milestone.

Freelancer sees the job as "funded" and starts work.

Funds are held in escrow and released upon completion.

